  "text": "Recipe: Yellow Mung Dal Idli Chaat\nCreator: Mrs N K Manku\nCategory: Chaat\nIngredients: mung dal, asafoetida (hing), Garbanzo beans (boiled), soy yogurt, Potatoes (boiled), Raw cabbage, Raw: tomatoes, capsicum, onion & beetroot, Dried cranberries, raisins, roasted cumin seeds powder, Green Chatni, Amla Dates Chatni, Sunflower seeds, pumpkin seeds, watermelon seeds, flaxseed powder\nCooking methods: soak, grind, stir, steam, no-cook\nInstructions: Soak mung dal for 4 to 6 hours. Grind it with minimum water. Stir it with fork to make a fluffy batter. Make small idlis out of the batter by steaming them in an Idli Maker. Put idlis in warm water with 1/2 tsp asafoetida (hing) for 10-15 mins. Squeeze them gently with palms to remove some water, like Dahi Bhalla. Place idlis in a serving bowl. Add toppings of your choice!\nNotes: Squeeze idlis gently with palms to remove some water, like Dahi Bhalla. Green Chatni and Amla Dates Chatni are components/sauces.",
